-8bcb-5b10-bade-10010a8005ac" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1fe65ee-e4c1-507a-9313-0ea6b012c1aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-126278" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- $A$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $1$ row and $1$ column, so it is a $1\\times 1$ matrix.\n\n- $B$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $3$ rows and $3$ columns, so it is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $C$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $1$ row and $2$ columns, so it's a $1\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are square matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b6ddadb-471a-5195-a0f5-fd44bdc8f780" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Other Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "778e7dac-5d43-5278-8a2c-8d400611b7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472562} {:answer/id #uuid "6090d412-485e-50cf-bfc7-d6f5ce1710e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "778e7dac-5d43-5278-8a2c-8d400611b7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 